3. Tone-mapping operators -- ALGORITHMS from papers, INDEPENDENT implementations
================================================================================

    hdr4rtt_rod/make_frontends.py implements the following published algorithms
    from their descriptions. No source code from these authors was used; the
    implementations are original work under this repository's MIT licence.
    Algorithms themselves are not subject to copyright, but the papers are cited
    because credit for the method belongs to their authors:

      Reinhard, Stark, Shirley, Ferwerda.
        Photographic Tone Reproduction for Digital Images. SIGGRAPH 2002.

      Durand, Dorsey.
        Fast Bilateral Filtering for the Display of High-Dynamic-Range Images.
        SIGGRAPH 2002.

    These implementations are simplified and were tuned against this dataset.
    They should NOT be treated as reference implementations of the published
    methods, and any shortcoming in them is this repository's, not the original
    authors'. In particular the Durand implementation computes its bilateral
    filter at reduced resolution and uses a percentile-based exposure step.

